a second set of human remains were found  at lake mead yesterday this comes less  than a week after a man's body was found  in a barrel on the lake shore decades  after police believe he was murdered  madison kimbrough joins us in the  newsroom with the latest in this latest  investigation madison i spoke with two  sisters who made this startling  discovery saturday afternoon along with  a retired henderson police officer who  is offering these women and anyone else  who finds additional remains a  5-thousand dollar reward  two bodies found in less than a week at  lake mead the first discovered in a  barrel and the second found saturday  afternoon in the sand at caulville bay  henderson locals lindsay melvin and her  sister lynette were paddle boarding when  they made the discovery at first i  thought it was a big horn sheep and we  kind of started digging around a little  bit as we discovered the jaw we realized  it was human remains and that's when we  contacted park rangers to come and  investigate for the longest time i was  in disbelief like i did not think that  we actually just came upon human remains  i thought that i was like this has to be  rocks this is still rocks it's rocks  nope it's definitely remains as of now  the clark county coroner's office is  working to identify the remains retired  henderson police officer david colemeyer  has been invested in what's been going  on and wanted to do something to help he  and his partner decided they would offer  a 5-thousand dollar reward to those who  find additional bodies at the lake he  says with this incentive he hopes it  will bring a sense of closure to the  families and friends of these victims  while assisting local law enforcement in  their efforts now it makes you start  thinking right like how many other  bodies will be recovered my feeling with  this particular situation it could be  more of a drowning person i think it's  not related to  the situation with the barrel but  definitely  something of major interest would be  nice to identify who this person is cole  meyer has currently set up a gofundme  page where people can donate funds to  help with burials  and we will have a contact for cole  meyer up on our website at 8newsnow.com  now as for saturday's finding sources  tell the 8 news now i-team there are no  signs of foul play and at this point  metro police are not involved in the  investigation live in the newsroom  madison kimbrough live local now
 

